WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.490
In 2014, Russia annexed Crimea.

2
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:08.570
In February 2022, it launched a
full-scale invasion of Ukraine.

3
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:14.770
On 25 February 2022, the UN Security Council
voted on a draft demanding that Russia

4
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.760
stop its attack and withdraw.

5
00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.620
Eleven voted for.

6
00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.650
Three abstained.

7
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.950
Russia voted against,
and the draft failed.

8
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.670
One permanent member's no blocked it.

9
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.850
So how else can Britain act over the war?

10
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.370
Could it use its own
veto to cancel Russia's?

11
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.310
In this mission, you'll see
how the Security Council works,

12
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.910
and why one vote can stop it.

13
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:41.670
Then you'll judge how much
influence Britain really has.

14
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:46.490
Your mission: find out how Britain can
still act when one veto blocks the Security

15
00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:47.390
Council.
